Setiap Anak mempunyai hak sebagai berikut:
a. hak hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang secara wajar sesual dengan harkat dan martabat kemanusiaannya, berpartisipasi dalam semua lapangan kehidupan,; memperoleh perlindungan dari tindakan diskriminasi; memperoleh perlindungan dari eksploitasi ekonomi dan seksual;
memperoleh perlindungan dari kekerasan fisik, psikologis, seksual dan penelantaran;
identitas kependudukan dan status kewerganegaraan;
f.
memperoleh akta kelahiran;
g.
memeluk agama dan beribadah menurut ajaran agama
h.
dan kepercayaannya dengan bantuan bimbingan orang tua/wali;
tidak dipaksa berganti agama oleh orang tua asuh, orang tua angkat dan oleh siapapun;
untuk diakui dan mengetahui orang tuanya, dibesarkan dan diasuh oleh orang tuanya sendiri;
k.
-14- memperoleh pelayanan kesehatan dan jaminan sosial sesuai dengan kebutuhan fisik, mental, spiritual, dan sosial;
memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran sesuai dengan minat dan bakatnya;
memperoleh perawatan, pendidikan, pelatihan, meningkatkan diri dan kemampuan berpartisipasi dalam kehidupan bermasyarakat dan bernegara bagi Anak penyandang disabilitas fisik, mental dan berkebutuhan khusus;
menyampaikan dan didengar pendapatnya;
beristirahat dan memanfaatkan waktu luang untuk pengembangan diri diluar jam sekolah;
memperoleh hak-hak lain sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
Article 11
Every Child has the following rights:
a. the right to live, grow and develop properly in accordance with human dignity, participate in all fields of life;
b. to obtain protection from discriminatory actions;
c. to obtain protection from economic and sexual exploitation;
d. to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence and neglect;
e. population identity and citizenship status;
f. to obtain a birth certificate;
g. to embrace religion and worship according to the teachings of religion
h. and their beliefs with the assistance of parental/guardian guidance;
i. not to be forced to change religion by foster parents, adoptive parents and by anyone;
j. to be recognized and know their parents, to be raised and cared for by their own parents;
k. -14- to obtain health services and social security in accordance with physical, mental, spiritual, and social needs;
l. to obtain education and teaching in accordance with their interests and talents;
m. to obtain care, education, training, self-improvement and the ability to participate in community and state life for Children with physical, mental disabilities and special needs;
n. to express and have their opinion heard;
o. to rest and utilize free time for self-development outside school hours;
p. to obtain other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

text:
Pasal 20
Sistem pemberdayaan Perempuan bertujuan untuk: os -17-
a. meningkatkan kualitas hidup Perempuan, dan Keluarga; b. meningkatkan kapasitas kelembagaan pemberdayaan Perempuan di Daerah, termasuk pengembangan sistem gendernya; dan
c. memberikan perlindungan hak Perempuan dari berbagai bentuk kekerasan dan perlakukan diskriminatif lainnya. Pasal 21 Dalam rangka mewujudkan tujuan meningkatkan kualitas hidup Perempuan, dan keluarga sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 huruf dilakukan melalui:
a. memberikan akses kepada Perempuan untuk menikmati layanan pendidikan, kesehatan, dan bidang strategis lainnya;
b. mendorong' keterlibatan Perempuan dalam proses pembangunan;
c. memberikan pengetahuan, keterampilan, nilai-nilai karakter, budi pekerti, dan ketahanan kKeluarga;
d. mendorong program-program yang dapat meningkatkan kemandirian Perempuan di bidang ekonomi, politik, hukum, sosial, budaya, serta bidang strategis lainnya; dan
e. memberikan kesempatan dan peluang kepada setiap Perempuan untuk menduduki berbagai posisi dan jabatan dalam berbagai lapangan pekerjaan, termasuk posisi stretegis sepanjang sesuai dengan kapasitas dan kemampuannya.

translated_text:
Article 20
The Women's empowerment system aims to: os -17-
a. improve the quality of life of Women, and Families; b. increase the institutional capacity of Women's empowerment in the Region, including the development of its gender system; and
c. provide protection of Women's rights from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment. Article 21 In order to realize the objective of improving the quality of life of Women, and families as referred to in Article 20 letter is carried out through:
a. providing access to Women to enjoy education services, health, and other strategic fields;
b. encouraging the involvement of Women in the development process;
c. providing knowledge, skills, character values, morals, and Family resilience;
d. encouraging programs that can increase Women's independence in the economic, political, legal, social, cultural fields, as well as other strategic fields; and
e. providing opportunities and chances to every Woman to occupy various positions and posts in various fields of work, including strategic positions as long as they are in accordance with her capacity and ability.

text:
Pasal 23
Dalam rangka menyelenggarakan tujuan memberikan perlindungan hak Perempuan dari berbagai bentuk kekerasan dan perlakukan diskriminatif lainnya sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 huruf dilakukan melalui: a. upaya promotif;
b. upaya preventif;
c. upaya kuratif; dan
d. wupaya rehabilitatif, sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
Article 23
In order to implement the objective of providing protection for Women's rights from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment as referred to in Article 20 letter, it shall be carried out through: a. promotive efforts;
b. preventive efforts;
c. curative efforts; and
d. rehabilitative efforts, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

text:
Pasal 27
Upaya rehabilitatif sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 23 huruf diselenggarakan dengan cara:
a. menyediakan tenaga pendamping bagi korban kejahatan dan kekerasan, yang meliputi antara lain: tenaga psikolog;
tenaga psikiater;
rohaniwan/pendamping spritual;
advokat;
tenaga media.
b. memperkuat jejaring kerja dan koordinasi dalam proses reintegrasi serta pemulangan korban kepada keluarga dan/atau lingkungan sosialnya.
Paragraf Pembentukan UPT PPA

translated_text:
Article 27
Rehabilitative efforts as referred to in Article 23 letter shall be implemented by means of:
a. providing accompanying personnel for victims of crime and violence, which includes among others: psychologists;
psychiatrists;
religious counselors/spiritual companions;
advocates;
media personnel.
b. strengthening work networks and coordination in the reintegration process as well as the return of victims to their families and/or social environment.
Paragraph Establishment of UPT PPA

text:
Pasal 34
Upaya peningkatan kapasitas Perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 43, dilakukan dalam berbagai bidang berikut ini:
a. ekonomi;
politik;
sosial;
budaya; dan hukum.

translated_text:
Article 34
Efforts to increase the capacity of Women as referred to in Article 43, are carried out in the following various fields:
a. economy;
b. politics;
c. social;
d. culture; and
e. law.

text:
Pasal 35
Peningkatan kapasitas Perempuan dalam bidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 34 huruf dilakukan dengan cara:
a.
b.
membanyak program pelatihan bagi Perempuan pelaku usaha;
mengupayakan secara maksimal agar Perempuan di Daerah mendapatkan akses permodalan melalui lembaga keuangan;
menyiapkan sistem permodalan alternatif bagi Perempuan pelaku ekonomi mikro di Daerah;
mengembangkan dukungan dana/sarana alternatif bagi Perempuan inovator; dan memberikan dan membantu memberikan akses pasar bagi produk-produk UMKM yang dihasilkan oleh Perempuan di Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 35
Capacity building for Women in the economic field as referred to in Article 34 letter is carried out by means of:
a.
b. increasing training programs for Women business actors;
making maximum efforts so that Women in the Region obtain access to capital through financial institutions;
preparing alternative capital systems for Women micro-economic actors in the Region;
developing alternative fund/facility support for Women innovators; and providing and assisting in providing market access for MSME products produced by Women in the Region.

text:
Pasal 36
Peningkatan kapasitas Perempuan dalam bidang politik sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 34 huruf dilakukan dengan cara:
a. memperbanyak program pelatihan penguatan peran politik Perempuan di Daerah;
memperbanyak sosialisasi tentang upaya peningkatan partisipasi politik Perempuan dalam pemilihan umum; menyiapkan sistem fasilitasi pengembangan diri Perempuan dalam berorganisasi, berserikat dan berkumpul di Daerah;
mengembangkan dukungan pada peningkatan kapasitas Perempuan dengan selalu melibatkannya dalam pengambilan keputusan yang menyangkut kepentingan Perempuan di Daerah; dan melaksanakan berbagai program yang dirasa mampu mendorong Perempuan untuk berani mengambil dan menduduki jabatan-jabatan publik yang terbuka untuk diemban oleh Perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 36
Capacity building for Women in the political field as referred to in Article 34 letter is carried out by means of:
a. increasing training programs for strengthening the political role of Women in the Region;
increasing socialization regarding efforts to enhance Women's political participation in general elections; preparing a facilitation system for Women's self-development in organizing, associating and assembling in the Region;
developing support for increasing Women's capacity by always involving them in decision-making concerning Women's interests in the Region; and implementing various programs deemed capable of encouraging Women to dare to take and occupy public positions that are open to be held by Women.

Article 37
Capacity building for Women in the social field as referred to in Article 34 letter is carried out by means of:
a. facilitating a Woman to access knowledge and technology for her future;
b. increasing socialization regarding efforts to improve Women's health, especially Women's reproductive health;
c. developing Women's participation in independent family planning, prosperous physically and spiritually;
d. encouraging every marriage conducted by a Woman to be officially recorded in State documents;
e. persuasively inviting Women in the Region not to conduct early marriage;
f. encouraging the continuous implementation of programs to reduce maternal mortality rates during childbirth; and
g. encouraging the formation and development of various organizations and various forums and coalitions of Women in the Region; and
h. making massive efforts so that cooperation between various Women's organizations in the Region develops well so as to be able to contribute concretely in the Region.

Article 38
Capacity building for Women in the cultural field as referred to in Article 34 letter d is carried out by means of:
a. facilitating every activity of Women related to culture, customs and traditions; and
b. preserving various cultures and local wisdom that can shape the character of Women into individuals who have strong and independent character in fighting for their lives.

Article 39
Capacity building for Women in the field of law as referred to in Article 34 letter shall be carried out by means of:
a. increasing socialization activities of various laws and regulations related to legal awareness of Women;
b. conducting mapping of adverse impacts due to weak understanding of Women in the field of law;
c. making policies that can minimize gender bias against Women; and
d. always involving and requesting the opinions of Women in the process of drafting and discussing legal products in the Region that are laden with the interests of Women.

text:
Pasal 42
Perlindungan Perempuan diselenggara-kan oleh Pemerintah Daerah dengan mengikutsertakan secara aktif berbagai komponen berikut:
a. Keluarga;
b. lembaga adat;
c. masyarakat; dan
d. organisasi kemasyarakatan.

translated_text:
Article 42
Protection of Women is organized by the Regional Government by actively involving the following various components:
a. Family;
b. customary institutions;
c. community; and
d. community organizations.

text:
Pasal 44
Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya perlindungan Perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 42 bertanggungjawab untuk melakukan hal-hal berikut:
a. merencanakan, membuat, menetapkan dan menyelenggarakan kebijakan, program dan Kkegiatan perlindungan Perempuan;
melakukan penguatan dan pengembangan lembaga penyedia layanan perlindungan Perempuan,;
secara dini melakukan berbagai upaya preventif agar kekerasan terhadap Perempuan tidak terjadi atau dapat diminimalisir;
secara massif dan berkelanjutan melakukan berbagai upaya agar tidak terjadi tindak kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dalam segala lapangan kehidupan;
secara massif dan berkelanjutan mencegah agar tidak terjadi TPPO; dan
f. secara berkesinambungan berupaya untuk melakukan perlindungan terhadap tenaga kerja Perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 44
Regional Government in the effort to protect Women as referred to in Article 42 is responsible for carrying out the following matters:
a. planning, making, establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women;
b. strengthening and developing institutions providing Women protection services;
c. early on carrying out various preventive efforts so that violence against Women does not occur or can be minimized;
d. massively and continuously carrying out various efforts so that acts of violence against Women do not occur in all fields of life;
e. massively and continuously preventing the occurrence of TPPO; and
f. continuously striving to provide protection for Women workers.

text:
Pasal 45
Agar upaya perlindungan Perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 44 terselenggara dengan baik, maka Pemerintah Daerah melakukan koordinasi, kerjasama dan bermitra dengan pihak-pihak berikut:
a. pemerintah pusat melalui instansi vertikal yang ada di Daerah;
pemerintah Kota/kota yang ada di provinsi Riau;
lembaga sosial dan keagamaan;
lembaga adat;
lembaga swadaya masyarakat;
f. perguruan tinggi; dan media.

translated_text:
Article 45
In order for the protection efforts for Women as referred to in Article 44 to be implemented properly, the Regional Government shall coordinate, cooperate and partner with the following parties:
a. the central government through vertical agencies in the Region;
b. City/city governments in Riau province;
c. social and religious institutions;
d. customary institutions;
e. non-governmental organizations;
f. universities; and
g. media.

